From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H96 build <builder@h96-build>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/59] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: CEC hardening and physical
 address from sink EDID

dw-hdmi-qp.c:
- cec-enable with a missing CEC irq warns and leaves video and audio
  up instead of failing the probe; only with CONFIG_DRM_DW_HDMI_CEC.
- the CEC irq is masked across suspend and restored on resume; the
  adapter is re-enabled on resume only if the CEC core has it enabled.
- hotplug EDID read for CEC is read-only (drm_edid_read_ddc()), since
  drm_get_edid() would update the connector property unlocked.
- physical address comes from the sink's own EDID read over DDC and is
  cached until the next HPD event; an override EDID carries another
  PA. Module parameter cec_phys_addr overrides it (0 = from the sink).

dw-hdmi-qp-cec.c:
- the adapter is published to the bridge only after
  cec_register_adapter(), and unpublished when the wake irq request
  fails or the device is removed.
- a resume re-enable keeps the claimed logical addresses.

Gated by DT: active only with cec-enable on the HDMI node.

H96 series: combination of 14f055b0a / d77c4ac14 (CEC hardening) and
92d353fd2 (CEC PA from sink EDID). Kept as one commit: the state
between both commits is not recoverable from the H96 source tree.

6.12 port: dw_hdmi_qp_cec_enable() on 6.12 takes cec_lock and calls
dw_hdmi_qp_cec_log_addr(INVALID) after unlock; the address restore is
written inside the locked block and the trailing reset dropped.
drm_edid_block_valid() is static on 6.12; replaced by a local header
and checksum check of each block read.
